  "result": "Excellent! All 125 tests pass. Here's a summary of the ID normalization implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've added customer ID normalization to handle mixed case and spaces in customer IDs:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/customers.js`**:\n   - Added `normalizeId()` function that:\n     - Trims whitespace: `' C-007 '` \u2192 `'C-007'`\n     - Converts to uppercase: `'c-007'` \u2192 `'C-007'`\n   - Updated `getCustomer()` to normalize the ID before lookup\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`**:\n   - Imported `normalizeId` from customers.js\n   - Updated `createInvoice()` to:\n     - Normalize the customerId before validation\n     - Store the normalized ID in the invoice object\n\n3. **Tests** (9 new tests):\n   - Added `normalizeId()` tests:\n     - Trimming whitespace\n     - Converting to uppercase\n     - Handling mixed case with spaces\n   - Added `getCustomer()` tests:\n     - Finding customers with lowercase IDs\n     - Finding customers with spaces around IDs\n     - Finding customers with mixed case and spaces\n   - Added `createInvoice()` tests:\n     - Storing normalized customer IDs (uppercase)\n     - Handling spaces in input IDs\n     - Handling mixed case input IDs\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- All customer ID comparisons use normalized IDs\n- Invoices store normalized customer IDs\n- Input like `'c-007 '` or `' C-007 '` are all treated as `'C-007'`\n- Works seamlessly with existing customer lookup and tier discount logic",
